-- title:
--   Canonical Gaussian fitted values and the structural support constant
-- statement:
--   Let \(\Theta\) be a nonempty compact metric space, let \(\vartheta:\Theta\to\mathbb R^d\) be continuous, and fix observations \(x_1,\ldots,x_n\). Form the positive fitted hull
--   \[
--   \mathcal C_x=\operatorname{conv}\left\{
--   \bigl(e^{\langle x_i,\vartheta(a)\rangle-\|\vartheta(a)\|^2/2}\bigr)_{i=1}^n:
--   a\in\Theta\right\}.
--   \]
--   For every real weight vector \(w\), the canonical fit selects a maximizer of
--   \(\sum_iw_i\log f_i\) over \(f\in\mathcal C_x\). Compactness guarantees existence even for weights that are not positive. This fitted vector uses the Gaussian scores after cancellation of the centered observation-density factors. The structural support coefficient is
--   \[
--   S_{d,C,b}=10^7\bigl(1+(4C+1)^d+(b+4)\bigr).
--   \]
-- source:
--   https://github.com/hanshengjiang/reweighted-npmle-lean/blob/5af8d16822c5a8a3f032b13eb95daea40f307484/ReweightedNPMLE/GaussianExactRegularization.lean#L18-L99

